[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was merged on subject lines ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject))
and marked known as one bug. Read by tenant and by what the reports say, it holds three problems.
Each has its own ticket. The counts below are computed from the export on every build, the way
[the #4471 table](/kb/incidents/4471) counts them.

<SplitTable ticket={4471} {tickets} />

<Callout kind="warn">
Engineering closed #4471 on 5 October: <code>parser</code> fixed (fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu
locales), <code>hint</code> won't fix (booking-v3 form retired). Neither touches <code>one-day</code>.
Closing #4471 does not close it: its ticket stays open.
</Callout>

## The three problems

**`parser` — the shared parser read every date month first.** Day-first tenants got day and month
swapped: "7 April" went out as "4 July". This is what #4471's title describes. Fixed.

**`hint` — booking-v3 printed `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field.** At day-first tenants on
booking-v3, people typed what the hint said, month first, and the form read it day first. It
looked like the parser bug in the reports, but the parser fix does not touch it. Won't fix: the
form is retired.

**`one-day` — the date moves by one day, not a month flip.** Tuesday shows as Monday, an invite
arrives before the booking, two clients in different time zones get different days for the same
meeting. That is a time-zone or day-boundary bug. The desk noted these reports
(`desk-notes.json`) and counts them where they are filed, under `parser`. The parser fix does not
reach them. Still open.

<Callout>
Do not count by intake tag. Intake guesses the cause from the reporter's browser; many reports
come from browsers set to <code>en-US</code> at day-first tenants. The cause follows the tenant's
locale, its booking form and the channel (<code>causes.ts</code>), and the "intake tag differs"
column shows how often the guess is wrong.
</Callout>

## How this was counted

1. Drop repeated rows: the export pages overlap, so one id counts once (`uniqueById`).
2. Place every report with `causeOf` (`groupByCause`): day-first tenant, `form` channel, booking-v3 →
   `hint`; any other day-first report → `parser`.
3. List the desk's one-day reports again as their own problem; they stay counted under `parser`, as
   the desk files them.

## What to change on the desk

- Split by cause, not subject. Same subject, different cause: keep apart. The
  [dedupe explorer](/kb/triage/dedupe) already shows the difference.
- When a big ticket is closed, check that its fixes cover every problem in it.

